    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d904">

                <pb facs="0856" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6455.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Cinclad
                            Juárez to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consul</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Ciudad Juárez</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Revolutionary conditions in this district generally do not improve as rapidly as
                    promised by the supporters of the new Government. Indications are that the
                    opposition army is larger than a month ago and that the Federal army is not so
                    strong.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
